WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:02.602
Readers always want to know:

2
00:00:02.602 --> 00:00:04.765
what period does this report cover?

3
00:00:04.765 --> 00:00:09.811
In this lesson, you will learn to show the earliest and latest dates in

4
00:00:09.811 --> 00:00:14.857
cards, switch between different date views, format them nicely, and start a date slicer.

5
00:00:14.857 --> 00:00:17.020
Let's put time on the page!

6
00:00:18.900 --> 00:00:23.032
On the Date and Time page, a card already shows the current time.

7
00:00:23.032 --> 00:00:27.800
I add a new card, and drop in the Date field from our calendar table.

8
00:00:38.400 --> 00:00:42.494
The card shows January first, two thousand twenty five, at midnight.

9
00:00:42.494 --> 00:00:46.960
For a date field, the card shows the Earliest date by default.

10
00:00:58.400 --> 00:01:03.480
I resize the card and move it next to the time card, so the page stays tidy.

11
00:01:10.400 --> 00:01:14.353
Right click the field in the visual to change the summary:

12
00:01:14.353 --> 00:01:16.509
Earliest, Latest, Count, or Count Distinct.

13
00:01:16.509 --> 00:01:21.180
You can also choose to show the Date, Year, Quarter, Month, or Day.

14
00:01:48.400 --> 00:01:52.226
Now I use the Ship date from the Shipments table.

15
00:01:52.226 --> 00:01:56.052
The card shows Monday, January second, two thousand twenty three:

16
00:01:56.052 --> 00:01:57.582
the earliest ship date.

17
00:01:57.582 --> 00:02:00.260
That tells readers where the data begins.

18
00:02:08.400 --> 00:02:12.866
In the Format pane, I adjust the callout value and the category label, so

19
00:02:12.866 --> 00:02:14.780
the date is easy to read.

20
00:02:28.400 --> 00:02:32.379
Next, I turn a visual into a slicer with the Ship date field.

21
00:02:32.379 --> 00:02:35.440
Readers will be able to pick their own date range.

22
00:02:53.400 --> 00:02:58.742
In the slicer's format settings, I set the font and size for the values.

23
00:02:58.742 --> 00:03:02.940
Dates in cards and slicers make every report clearer. Nice job!

